=begin
    elogin.lic: A script for logging into other characters from within lich.

    Useful for switching characters or logging into characters on other accounts.

  Usage:
    ;elogin help                                            # Show usage
    ;elogin list                                            # List saved characters
    ;elogin set realm <prime|platinum|shattered|test>       # Set game realm
    ;elogin <char> [script1,script2]                        # Login with optional scripts
    ;elogin <char> --custom-launch=warlock                  # Login with custom launcher
    ;elogin <char> --saga                                   # Login via the Saga frontend
    ;elogin add <char> <user_id> [<password>] [--frontend=<name>] [--custom-launch=<launcher>]
                                                             # Add character entry; password may be omitted when
                                                             # <user_id> already has a saved account
    ;elogin delete <char> <game_code> [frontend]            # Delete character entry (frontend disambiguates duplicates)
    ;elogin modify <char> <account> <password> [--frontend=<name>] [--show-password]
                                                             # Modify character entry; --frontend disambiguates when the
                                                             # char/account has multiple entries, --show-password reveals
                                                             # the old password after an explicit pause/unpause confirmation

             author: elanthia-online
       contributors: Phalen33, Lucullan
               game: Gemstone
               tags: login
           required: Lich >= 5.20.1
            version: 2.1.0

  2.1.0 (2026-08-30)
    - Add support for logging in with the Saga frontend
    - Add a --show-password option to `modify` to view a saved password
    - Support saving more than one login per character (e.g. one for Saga,
      one for another frontend); `add`, `modify`, and `delete` can now be
      told which one to use with a frontend option
    - Fix a bug where a saved password could show up in the debug log
    - Fix a couple of bugs with `delete` and `modify` around multiple saved
      logins for the same character
    - Fix: changing a password with `modify` now updates it everywhere that
      account is saved, not just for the one character you named
    - Fix: logging in could occasionally get blocked by a custom launcher
      setting saved under a different login for the same character
    - Adding a new character to an account you've already saved no longer
      needs the password again
    - Show a clear error up front if you try to launch Saga for a character
      that doesn't have a login saved specifically for Saga, instead of
      quietly failing in the launched window
    - Internal cleanup and documentation
  2.0.4 (2026-03-31)
    - Correctly spawn login to support GTK dark_mode theme settings
  2.0.3 (2026-02-26)
    - Update to new API calls for Lich 5.15
  2.0.2 (2026-02-26)
    - Resolve error when the only Lich entry was for a custom launch. Will default to whichever the first saved character entry is when no frontend is given.
  2.0.1 (2026-01-17)
    - Adds support for custom launch commands
  2.0.0 (2026-01-13)
    - Adds support for Lich 5.13 and beyond
  1.2.3 (2024-12-02)
    - Wrap RUBY & LICH location path in quotes incase of spaces in path
  1.2.2 (2024-11-24)
    - Remove references to ;trust script, deprecated
  1.2.1 (2024-10-10)
    - Anchor regex comparisons and convert to_s
  1.2.0 (2024-07-22)
    - Add support for GSTest instance
  1.1.3 (2023-11-15)
    - Change ruby process launching from using system() to Process.spawn()
  1.1.2 (2023-03-28)
    - Change from using SAL login method to native character saved entry CLI login method
  1.1.1 (2023-01-23)
    - Update for Ruby v3 compatibility
  1.1.0 (2022-02-01)
    - Fix for Wrayth login method
    - Add Lich version check
  1.0.0 (2015-09-19)
    - Initial release
=end

module ELogin
  LICH_GEM_REQUIRES = '5.20.1'

  # ============================================================================
  # HELPER METHODS
  # ============================================================================

  # Emits a message only when Lich's debug messaging is enabled. Never pass
  # secrets (passwords) here -- it is visible in the game window/log.
  # @param message [#to_s]
  # @return [void]
  def self.debug_log(message)
    return unless Lich.debug_messaging
    Lich::Messaging.msg('debug', "#{message}")
  end

  # Reports an error to the player and the Lich log, optionally exiting.
  # @param message [String]
  # @param should_exit [Boolean] whether to terminate the script after reporting
  # @return [void]
  def self.handle_error(message, should_exit: true)
    echo message
    Lich.log "elogin error: #{message}" if defined?(Lich)
    exit if should_exit
  end

  # Records a routine (non-error) action to the Lich log.
  # @param message [String]
  # @return [void]
  def self.log_operation(message)
    Lich.log "elogin: #{message}" if defined?(Lich)
  end

  # Guards against a malformed entry-store load. Exits via {handle_error} when
  # +entry_data+ is not an Array.
  # @param entry_data [Object] value returned by {load_entry_data}
  # @return [void]
  def self.ensure_entry_data!(entry_data)
    handle_error("Fatal: entry_data was not loaded correctly. Got #{entry_data.class} instead of Array.") unless entry_data.is_a?(Array)
  end

  # Finds the first frontend override flag among +args+ (e.g. +--saga+,
  # +--stormfront+, +--frontend=saga+). Matches
  # +LoginHelpers::FRONTEND_PATTERN+ directly so new frontends Lich adds are
  # picked up automatically.
  # @param args [Array<String>]
  # @return [String, nil] the matched frontend name, downcased, or nil
  def self.extract_frontend_flag(args)
    pattern = Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers::FRONTEND_PATTERN
    args.each do |arg|
      return $~[:fe].downcase if arg =~ pattern
    end
    nil
  end

  # Finds a +--custom-launch=<value>+ flag among +args+.
  # @param args [Array<String>]
  # @return [String, nil] the launcher value, or nil if not present
  def self.extract_custom_launch_flag(args)
    args.each do |arg|
      return $1 if arg =~ /^--custom-launch=(.+)$/i
    end
    nil
  end

  # Loads saved login entries from entry.yaml and converts to legacy entry hashes.
  # Lich 5.15+ uses YAML-backed saved entries only.
  # @return [Array<Hash>] saved entries in legacy hash format
  def self.load_entry_data
    load_yaml_entries
  end

  # Reads entry.yaml directly and converts it to the legacy entry-hash format
  # via {Lich::Common::Authentication::EntryStore}. Exits via {handle_error}
  # when the file is missing or fails to parse.
  # @return [Array<Hash>]
  def self.load_yaml_entries
    yaml_path = Lich::Common::Authentication::EntryStore.yaml_file_path(DATA_DIR)
    debug_log("Looking for YAML file at: #{yaml_path}")
    debug_log("YAML file exists: #{File.exist?(yaml_path)}")

    handle_error("Error: no saved entries YAML file found at #{yaml_path}") unless File.exist?(yaml_path)

    begin
      raw_yaml = YAML.load_file(yaml_path)
      debug_log("Raw YAML loaded: #{raw_yaml.class} with keys: #{raw_yaml.keys if raw_yaml.respond_to?(:keys)}")
      accounts = raw_yaml.is_a?(Hash) ? raw_yaml['accounts'] : nil
      debug_log("Raw YAML accounts: #{accounts.respond_to?(:count) ? accounts.count : 'none'} records.")

      legacy_format = Lich::Common::Authentication::EntryStore.convert_yaml_to_legacy_format(raw_yaml)
      debug_log("Legacy format result: #{legacy_format.class} with #{legacy_format.length} entries")

      legacy_format
    rescue => e
      debug_log("Error in YAML loading: #{e.class} - #{e.message}")
      handle_error("Error loading entry.yaml: #{e.class} - #{e.message}")
    end
  end

  # Persists entry hashes through EntryStore which handles legacy-format conversion.
  # @param entry_data [Array<Hash>]
  # @return [void]
  def self.save_entry_data(entry_data)
    # Debug: Show what we're trying to save
    debug_log("About to save #{entry_data.length} entries")
    entry_data.each_with_index do |entry, i|
      debug_log("Entry #{i}: #{entry[:char_name]} (#{entry[:game_code]})")
    end

    success = Lich::Common::Authentication::EntryStore.save_entries(DATA_DIR, entry_data)
    debug_log("Save result: #{success}")
    handle_error("Error: Failed to save to entry.yaml") unless success
  end

  # Resolves login_helpers source paths for Lich 5.15+ layout.
  # @param mode [String] "production" or "beta"; selects the remote branch
  #   used as a fallback source
  # @return [Hash{Symbol=>String}] :local_path, :require_path, :remote_url
  def self.resolve_login_helpers_paths(mode = 'production')
    case mode
    when "production"
      remote_repo = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elanthia-online/lich-5/main/lib"
    when "beta"
      remote_repo = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elanthia-online/lich-5/staging/lib"
    else
      handle_error("Unknown mode: #{mode.inspect}")
    end

    local_path = File.join(LIB_DIR, 'common', 'authentication', 'login_helpers.rb')
    require_path = File.join(LIB_DIR, 'common', 'authentication', 'login_helpers')

    remote_url = "#{remote_repo}/common/authentication/login_helpers.rb"
    { local_path: local_path, require_path: require_path, remote_url: remote_url }
  end

  # Ensures login_helpers.rb is present locally, downloading it from the
  # lich-5 GitHub repo when it's missing, then requires it.
  # @param mode [String] "production" or "beta"
  # @return [void]
  def self.ensure_login_helpers_loaded(mode = 'production')
    paths = resolve_login_helpers_paths(mode)

    unless File.exist?(paths[:local_path])
      if paths[:remote_url]
        begin
          require 'net/http'
          require 'uri'

          uri = URI(paths[:remote_url])
          response = Net::HTTP.get_response(uri)

          if response.code == '200'
            content = response.body
            FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(paths[:local_path]))
            File.write(paths[:local_path], content)
          else
            handle_error("Failed to download login_helpers.rb: HTTP #{response.code}")
          end
        rescue => e
          handle_error("Failed to download login_helpers.rb from #{paths[:remote_url]}: #{e.message}")
        end
      else
        handle_error("No valid source found to populate login_helpers.rb")
      end
    end

    require paths[:require_path]
  end

  # Adds a new saved login entry and persists it to entry.yaml.
  #
  # A character may have more than one saved entry for the same game_code as
  # long as they differ by frontend (e.g. a Wrayth entry and a Saga entry for
  # the same character/instance); the duplicate check below is scoped
  # accordingly so that combination is allowed. Exits via {handle_error} when
  # an entry for the same character, game_code, and frontend already exists,
  # or when the frontend/custom_launch combination violates
  # {Lich::Common::SagaLaunchPolicy}.
  #
  # +password+ may be omitted when adding another character to an account
  # that already has at least one saved entry: EntryStore stores one password
  # per account (keyed off the first entry it sees for that account_id), so
  # the account's existing saved password is reused automatically. A password
  # is still required the first time an account is saved.
  #
  # @param entry_data [Array<Hash>] loaded via {load_entry_data}, mutated in place
  # @param char_name [String]
  # @param user_id [String] account name
  # @param password [String, nil] required unless +user_id+ already has a
  #   saved entry in +entry_data+
  # @param game_code [String, nil] defaults to the game code for the current
  #   +CharSettings['realm']+
  # @param game_name [String]
  # @param frontend [String, Symbol, nil] defaults to the running session's +$frontend+
  # @param custom_launch [String, nil]
  # @param custom_launch_dir [String, nil]
  # @return [void]
  def self.add_login_entry(entry_data, char_name:, user_id:, password: nil, game_code: nil, game_name: 'GemStone IV', frontend: $frontend, custom_launch: nil, custom_launch_dir: nil)
    ensure_entry_data!(entry_data)

    if Lich::Common::SagaLaunchPolicy.custom_launch_conflict?(frontend: frontend, custom_launch: custom_launch)
      handle_error("Error: #{Lich::Common::SagaLaunchPolicy::CUSTOM_LAUNCH_CONFLICT}")
    end

    if password.to_s.strip.empty?
      account_known = entry_data.any? { |d| d[:user_id].to_s.casecmp?(user_id) }
      unless account_known
        handle_error("Error: Add failed. A password is required to save a new account (#{user_id}). Once it's saved, you can add more characters to the same account without repeating the password.")
      end
    end

    # Debug: Show what we loaded
    debug_log("Loaded #{entry_data.length} existing entries")
    entry_data.each_with_index do |entry, i|
      debug_log("Existing Entry #{i}: #{entry[:char_name]} (#{entry[:game_code]})")
    end

    game_code ||= case CharSettings['realm']
                  when 'platinum' then 'GSX'
                  when 'shattered' then 'GSF'
                  when 'test' then 'GST'
                  else 'GS3'
                  end

    existing = entry_data.find do |d|
      d[:char_name].casecmp?(char_name) && d[:game_code] == game_code && d[:frontend].to_s.casecmp?(frontend.to_s)
    end
    if existing
      handle_error("Error: Add failed. Character already exists for #{char_name} (#{game_code}, #{frontend}). Use `modify` to update or `delete` to remove existing entry.")
    end

    # Use exact structure from original legacy code
    h = {
      :char_name         => char_name,
      :game_code         => game_code,
      :game_name         => game_name,
      :user_id           => user_id.downcase,
      :password          => password,
      :frontend          => frontend,
      :custom_launch     => custom_launch,
      :custom_launch_dir => custom_launch_dir
    }
    entry_data.push(h)

    debug_log("After adding new entry, total entries: #{entry_data.length}")

    save_entry_data(entry_data)
    log_operation("Added login entry for #{char_name} (#{game_code}) with account #{user_id}")
    echo "Successfully added login entry for #{char_name} (#{game_code})."
  end

  # Updates the password for a saved account. Since the account's password is
  # a single value shared by every character saved under it, every entry
  # matching +user_id+ is updated -- not only the entry located via
  # +char_name+, which exists solely to validate the account/character pair
  # and (for +show_password+) to identify which entry's password to reveal.
  # When a character/account pair has more than one saved entry (distinguished
  # by frontend), +frontend:+ is required to pick which one to validate
  # against; otherwise this exits via {handle_error}.
  #
  # @param entry_data [Array<Hash>] loaded via {load_entry_data}, mutated in place
  # @param char_name [String]
  # @param user_id [String] account name identifying the entry to update
  # @param password [String] new password to store
  # @param show_password [Boolean] when true, reveal the entry's current
  #   saved password after an explicit warning and a script pause/unpause
  #   confirmation (see {Lich::Common::Script#pause})
  # @param frontend [String, Symbol, nil] disambiguates which entry to update
  #   when more than one matches +char_name+/+user_id+
  # @return [void]
  def self.modify_login_entry(entry_data, char_name:, user_id:, password:, show_password: false, frontend: nil)
    ensure_entry_data!(entry_data)

    # Find existing entries by character name AND account (user_id); a
    # character can have more than one entry here if they differ by frontend.
    matching_entries = entry_data.select { |d| d[:char_name].casecmp?(char_name) && d[:user_id].casecmp?(user_id) }

    if matching_entries.empty?
      echo "Modify failed. No entry found for character: #{char_name} with account: #{user_id}"
      echo "Existing characters:"
      entry_data.each { |entry| echo "  #{entry[:char_name]} (#{entry[:game_code]}) - #{entry[:user_id]}" }
      handle_error("Character/account combination not found.")
    end

    if matching_entries.size > 1 && (frontend.nil? || frontend == :__unset)
      handle_error("Modify failed. Multiple entries exist for #{char_name} (#{user_id}). Specify --frontend=<name> to update a precise record.")
    end

    existing = frontend.nil? || frontend == :__unset ? matching_entries.first : matching_entries.find { |d| d[:frontend].to_s.casecmp?(frontend.to_s) }
    handle_error("Modify failed. No entry found for #{char_name} (#{user_id}) with frontend #{frontend}.") unless existing

    # Never interpolate `existing` wholesale here -- it contains the plaintext password.
    debug_log("Found existing entry: #{existing[:char_name]} (#{existing[:game_code]}) - #{existing[:user_id]}")

    if show_password
      echo "WARNING: this will display the CURRENT saved password for #{existing[:char_name]} (#{existing[:user_id]}) in plain text in this window/log."
      echo "Unpause this script (;unpause #{Script.current.name}) to reveal it, or kill the script now to cancel."
      Script.current.pause
      echo "Saved password for #{existing[:char_name]} (#{existing[:user_id]}): #{existing[:password]}"
    end

    # EntryStore stores one password per account (keyed off the first entry
    # it sees for that account when flattening back to YAML), so every saved
    # entry for this account needs the new password -- not just the entry
    # located above -- or a sibling character's stale copy could win when
    # re-saved even though this reports success.
    entry_data.each { |d| d[:password] = password if d[:user_id].to_s.casecmp?(user_id) }

    save_entry_data(entry_data)
    log_operation("Modified login entry for #{char_name} with account #{user_id}")
    echo "Successfully modified login entry for #{char_name} with account #{user_id}."
  end

  # Prints a table of saved entries (account, character, instance, frontend).
  # @param entry_data [Array<Hash>]
  # @return [void]
  def self.list_login_entries(entry_data)
    ensure_entry_data!(entry_data)

    if entry_data.empty?
      echo "No saved character entries found."
      return
    end

    saved_entries = Terminal::Table.new(:headings => ['Account', 'Character', 'Instance', 'Frontend'])
    entry_data.each_with_index do |entry, _i|
      account = entry[:user_id].to_s
      character = entry[:char_name].to_s
      instance = entry[:game_code].to_s
      frontend = entry[:frontend].to_s
      saved_entries.add_row([account, character, instance, frontend])
    end
    respond saved_entries
    echo "Total: #{entry_data.length} entries"
  end

  # Deletes a saved login entry matching character and game_code. When more
  # than one entry matches (they differ by frontend), +frontend:+ is required
  # to disambiguate; this reports the error and returns false rather than exiting.
  # @param entry_data [Array<Hash>] loaded via {load_entry_data}, mutated in place
  # @param char_name [String]
  # @param game_code [String]
  # @param frontend [String, Symbol, nil] disambiguates which entry to delete
  #   when more than one matches +char_name+/+game_code+
  # @return [Boolean] true if an entry was deleted, false on failure
  def self.delete_login_entry(entry_data, char_name:, game_code:, frontend: nil)
    matching_entries = entry_data.select do |entry|
      entry[:char_name].casecmp?(char_name) && entry[:game_code].to_s.casecmp?(game_code.to_s)
    end

    if matching_entries.empty?
      handle_error("Delete failed. No matching entry found for #{char_name} (#{game_code}).", should_exit: false)
      return false
    end

    if matching_entries.size > 1 && (frontend.nil? || frontend == :__unset)
      handle_error("Delete failed. Multiple entries exist for #{char_name} (#{game_code}). Specify frontend to delete a precise record.", should_exit: false)
      return false
    end

    target = if frontend.nil? || frontend == :__unset
               matching_entries.first
             else
               matching_entries.find { |entry| entry[:frontend].to_s.casecmp?(frontend.to_s) }
             end

    unless target
      handle_error("Delete failed. No entry for #{char_name} (#{game_code}) with frontend #{frontend}.", should_exit: false)
      return false
    end

    entry_data.reject! { |entry| entry.equal?(target) }

    save_entry_data(entry_data)
    log_operation("Deleted login entry for #{char_name} (#{game_code})")
    echo "Deleted entry and saved YAML."
    true
  end

  # Prints the command usage summary.
  # @return [void]
  def self.show_usage
    echo "Usage:"
    echo "  ;elogin set realm <prime|platinum|shattered|test>"
    echo "  ;elogin <char> --custom-launch=<launcher>         # e.g., --custom-launch=warlock"
    echo "  ;elogin <char> --saga                             # launch via the Saga frontend"
    echo "  ;elogin <char> [script1,script2,...]"
    echo "  ;elogin add <char> <user_id> [<password>] [--frontend=<name>] [--custom-launch=<launcher>]"
    echo "  ;elogin modify <char> <user_id> <password> [--frontend=<name>] [--show-password]"
    echo "  ;elogin delete <char> <game_code> [frontend]"
    echo "  ;elogin list"
  end

  # Parses the raw script arguments into a command hash for {run} to dispatch on.
  # @param args [Array<String>] +Script.current.vars+-style argument list
  # @return [Hash] always includes :command (one of :help, :set_realm,
  #   :add_entry, :modify_entry, :list_entries, :delete_entry, :login); the
  #   remaining keys vary by command (e.g. :char_name, :frontend, :scripts)
  def self.parse_arguments(args)
    # Clean redundant arguments from Lich command processing
    args.shift if args.size >= 2 && args[0].is_a?(String) && args[1].is_a?(String) && args[0] == args[1..].join(' ')

    return { command: :help } if args.empty? || args[0] =~ /^help$/i

    case args[0].to_s.downcase
    when 'set'
      if args[1] =~ /^realm$/i && args[2]
        { command: :set_realm, realm: args[2].to_s.downcase }
      else
        { command: :help }
      end
    when 'add'
      if args.length >= 3
        # Password is optional when adding another character to an
        # already-saved account, so args[3] is only a password if it's not
        # itself a flag (e.g. `;elogin add Char account --frontend=saga`).
        if args[3] && !args[3].start_with?('--')
          password = args[3]
          extra_args = args[4..] || []
        else
          password = nil
          extra_args = args[3..] || []
        end
        {
          command: :add_entry,
          char_name: args[1].capitalize,
          user_id: args[2].downcase,
          password: password,
          frontend: extract_frontend_flag(extra_args),
          custom_launch: extract_custom_launch_flag(extra_args)
        }
      else
        { command: :help }
      end
    when 'modify'
      if args.length >= 4
        extra_args = args[4..] || []
        {
          command: :modify_entry,
          char_name: args[1].capitalize,
          user_id: args[2].downcase,
          password: args[3],
          frontend: extract_frontend_flag(extra_args),
          show_password: extra_args.any? { |a| a =~ /^--show-password$/i }
        }
      else
        { command: :help }
      end
    when 'list'
      { command: :list_entries }
    when 'delete'
      if args.length >= 3
        { command: :delete_entry, char_name: args[1], game_code: args[2], frontend: args[3] }
      else
        { command: :help }
      end
    else
      # Login command - extract character name, instance flag, and scripts
      char_name = args[0]&.capitalize

      # Extract custom-launch filter (--custom-launch=VALUE)
      custom_launch_filter = extract_custom_launch_flag(args)

      # Extract frontend flag (--stormfront, --wizard, --avalon, --saga, --frontend=saga, ...)
      frontend_flag = extract_frontend_flag(args)

      # Extract instance flag (--GST, --DR, --GSF, etc.)
      instance_flag = :__unset
      args.each do |arg|
        if arg.start_with?('--')
          flag = arg.sub('--', '').upcase
          if Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers::VALID_GAME_CODES.include?(flag)
            instance_flag = flag
            break
          end
        end
      end

      # Remove instance flag from args and extract scripts
      # Also remove frontend flag and custom-launch from consideration
      args_without_flags = args.reject do |arg|
        arg == "--#{instance_flag}" ||
          arg =~ Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers::FRONTEND_PATTERN ||
          arg =~ /^--custom-launch=/i
      end
      scripts = args_without_flags[1]&.split(',')&.map(&:strip) || []

      { command: :login, char_name: char_name, instance_flag: instance_flag, scripts: scripts, custom_launch: custom_launch_filter, frontend: frontend_flag }
    end
  end

  # ============================================================================
  # MAIN EXECUTION
  # ============================================================================

  # Entry point: loads Lich's login helpers, parses the script's arguments,
  # and dispatches to the matching command (list/add/modify/delete/login/etc).
  # @return [void]
  def self.run
    # Setup environment
    ensure_login_helpers_loaded(ENV['LICH_MODE'] || 'production')

    # Lich 5.15+ uses EntryStore YAML backend.
    require File.join(LIB_DIR, 'common', 'authentication', 'entry_store')

    # Needed to preflight the Saga + --custom-launch conflict before spawning.
    require File.join(LIB_DIR, 'common', 'saga_launch_policy')

    # Parse arguments
    parsed = parse_arguments(Script.current.vars.dup)

    # Execute command
    case parsed[:command]
    when :help
      show_usage

    when :set_realm
      valid_realms = %w[prime platinum shattered test]
      unless valid_realms.include?(parsed[:realm])
        handle_error("Invalid realm. Use: prime, platinum, shattered, or test.")
      end

      CharSettings['realm'] = parsed[:realm]
      log_operation("Set realm to #{parsed[:realm]}")
      echo "Realm set to #{parsed[:realm]}."

    when :add_entry
      entry_data = load_entry_data
      add_login_entry(entry_data,
                      char_name: parsed[:char_name],
                      user_id: parsed[:user_id],
                      password: parsed[:password],
                      frontend: parsed[:frontend] || $frontend,
                      custom_launch: parsed[:custom_launch])

    when :modify_entry
      entry_data = load_entry_data
      modify_login_entry(entry_data,
                         char_name: parsed[:char_name],
                         user_id: parsed[:user_id],
                         password: parsed[:password],
                         frontend: parsed[:frontend],
                         show_password: parsed[:show_password])

    when :list_entries
      entry_data = load_entry_data
      list_login_entries(entry_data)

    when :delete_entry
      entry_data = load_entry_data
      delete_login_entry(entry_data,
                         char_name: parsed[:char_name],
                         game_code: parsed[:game_code],
                         frontend: parsed[:frontend])

    when :login
      # Validate realm is set
      realm = CharSettings['realm']
      handle_error("No realm set. Use ;elogin set realm <prime|platinum|shattered|test>") unless realm

      # Load entry data
      entry_data = load_entry_data

      # Determine game code
      game_code = if parsed[:instance_flag] == :__unset
                    Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers.realm_to_game_code(realm)
                  else
                    parsed[:instance_flag]
                  end

      # Find character
      char_records = Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers.find_character_by_name_and_game(
        entry_data, parsed[:char_name], game_code
      )

      # requested_fe matters even with only one character/instance match: when
      # that character has multiple saved entries differing by frontend (e.g.
      # a Wrayth entry with a stored custom_launch alongside a plain Saga
      # entry), select_best_fit breaks ties by array order when no frontend
      # is requested -- silently applying a sibling's custom_launch to a
      # login that never asked for one.
      char_entry = Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers.select_best_fit(
        char_data_sets: char_records,
        requested_character: parsed[:char_name],
        requested_instance: game_code.to_s,
        requested_fe: parsed[:frontend] || :__unset
      )

      handle_error("No matching entry found for #{parsed[:char_name]} in realm #{realm}.") unless char_entry

      # Determine instance override
      realm_game_code = Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers.realm_to_game_code(realm)
      # Determine instance override: CLI arg takes precedence
      instance_override = if parsed[:instance_flag] != :__unset
                            parsed[:instance_flag]
                          elsif char_entry[:game_code] == realm_game_code
                            char_entry[:game_code]
                          else
                            char_entry[:_requested_game_code]
                          end

      # Determine effective custom launch (stored value becomes default)
      effective_custom_launch = parsed[:custom_launch]
      if effective_custom_launch.nil? && char_entry[:custom_launch] && !char_entry[:custom_launch].to_s.empty?
        effective_custom_launch = char_entry[:custom_launch]
      end

      # If using custom launch, do NOT force a frontend
      frontend_override =
        if effective_custom_launch
          parsed[:frontend] || :__unset
        else
          parsed[:frontend] || char_entry[:frontend]
        end

      # Saga owns its own authentication/launch and is incompatible with Custom Launch.
      if Lich::Common::SagaLaunchPolicy.custom_launch_conflict?(frontend: frontend_override, custom_launch: effective_custom_launch)
        handle_error("Error: #{Lich::Common::SagaLaunchPolicy::CUSTOM_LAUNCH_CONFLICT}")
      end

      # Lich's Saga-managed launch requires a saved entry tagged frontend:
      # saga for this exact character/instance -- it will not accept any
      # other saved entry, even one with matching credentials under a
      # different frontend. Catch that here so it surfaces as a clear error
      # instead of a silent no-op in the spawned (and detached) process.
      if frontend_override.to_s.casecmp?('saga')
        login_game_code = (instance_override || char_entry[:game_code]).to_s
        saga_entry_exists = entry_data.any? do |d|
          d[:char_name].casecmp?(char_entry[:char_name]) &&
            d[:game_code].to_s.casecmp?(login_game_code) &&
            d[:frontend].to_s.casecmp?('saga')
        end
        unless saga_entry_exists
          handle_error("Error: No saved entry for #{char_entry[:char_name]} (#{login_game_code}) is tagged for the Saga frontend, so Lich will refuse this login even though an entry exists under a different frontend. Add one with: ;elogin add #{char_entry[:char_name]} #{char_entry[:user_id]} --frontend=saga (no password needed -- that account is already saved)")
        end
      end

      ruby_path =
        if OS.windows?
          ruby_dir = File.dirname(RbConfig.ruby)
          ruby_executable = File.basename(RbConfig.ruby)
          rubyw_executable = ruby_executable.sub(/^ruby(?=\.|$)/, 'rubyw')
          File.join(ruby_dir, rubyw_executable)
        else
          RbConfig.ruby
        end
      lich_path = File.join(LICH_DIR, 'lich.rbw')

      spawn_cmd = [
        ruby_path,
        lich_path,
        '--login', char_entry[:char_name]
      ]

      if instance_override
        flag = Lich::Common::Authentication::LoginHelpers.format_launch_flag(instance_override)
        spawn_cmd << flag if flag
      end

      spawn_cmd << "--#{frontend_override}" if frontend_override && frontend_override != :__unset
      spawn_cmd << "--custom-launch=#{effective_custom_launch}" if effective_custom_launch
      spawn_cmd << "--start-scripts=#{parsed[:scripts].join(',')}" if parsed[:scripts].any?

      if Lich.respond_to?(:track_dark_mode)
        spawn_cmd << "--dark-mode=#{Lich.track_dark_mode}"
      end

      Lich::Messaging.msg('info', "Spawning login: #{spawn_cmd}")
      debug_log("Spawning login: #{spawn_cmd.inspect}")

      begin
        pid = Process.spawn(*spawn_cmd)
        Process.detach(pid)
        echo "Launched #{char_entry[:char_name]} in a separate process (pid #{pid}). elogin can't see what happens after handoff -- if it doesn't connect, check that process's own window/log for the actual error."
      rescue Errno::ENOENT => e
        handle_error("Executable not found: #{e.message}", should_exit: false)
      rescue StandardError => e
        handle_error("Failed to launch login session: #{e.class} - #{e.message}", should_exit: false)
      end
    end
  end
end

if Gem::Version.new(LICH_VERSION) < Gem::Version.new(ELogin::LICH_GEM_REQUIRES)
  echo "elogin.lic requires Lich v#{ELogin::LICH_GEM_REQUIRES}+."
  exit
end

ELogin.run
